    "created_at": "2019-09-07T18:27:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-07T18:27:14Z",
    "body": "I think everything should have a sane default :)\r\n\r\nBut yes, agreed. I think something around 1-2 seconds would be reasonable for most modern computers (made past 2015), and users who operate on older hardware or in unusual circumstances can set it if they wish to.\r\n\r\nThat number comes from the fact that when working with a very dirty copy of the LLVM repo on a (rather cheap) thinkpad from 2017, the git status module takes a little over a second to fire the first time and somewhere between 300-500ms after that (assuming the caches remain warm). ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
